   2          /**
   3           * @file
   4           * SNMP output message processing (RFC1157).
   5           *
   6           * Output responses and traps are build in two passes:
   7           *
   8           * Pass 0: iterate over the output message backwards to determine encoding lengths
   9           * Pass 1: the actual forward encoding of internal form into ASN1
  10           *
  11           * The single-pass encoding method described by Comer & Stevens
  12           * requires extra buffer space and copying for reversal of the packet.
  13           * The buffer requirement can be prohibitively large for big payloads
  14           * (>= 484) therefore we use the two encoding passes.
  15           */
